---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { journal, ojs, contact } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="For Reviewers"
  description="Guidelines for peer reviewers of the Algerian Journal of Applied Mathematics — review criteria, process, confidentiality, and how to write a constructive report."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Peer review"
    title="For Reviewers"
    subtitle="Expert peer review is the foundation of scientific integrity. AJAM is grateful to every reviewer who donates their time and expertise to uphold the quality of applied mathematics research."
  />

  <!-- ─────────────────────────── Introduction & CTAs ─────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">

      <p class="lead">
        The <em>{journal.title}</em> operates a rigorous <strong>double-blind peer review</strong>
        process in which neither authors nor reviewers know each other's identities. Reviewers are
        the backbone of AJAM's quality assurance: your expert judgement ensures that only
        scientifically sound, original, and clearly presented work reaches our readership.
        We sincerely thank every colleague who contributes to this mission.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href={ojs.login} class="btn btn--primary">Reviewer login</a>
        <a href={ojs.register} class="btn btn--gold">Register as a reviewer</a>
      </div>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- ─────────────────── What we ask you to evaluate ─────────────────── -->
      <h2>What We Ask You to Evaluate</h2>
      <p>
        When assessing a submission, reviewers should address the following dimensions.
        Not every criterion will be equally relevant to every paper — use your judgement
        and indicate clearly which aspects most influenced your recommendation.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid--3">

        <div class="card card--accent">
          <p class="criterion-icon">★</p>
          <h3 class="criterion-title">Originality &amp; Significance</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Does the work make a genuine new contribution? Is the result, method, or
            application meaningful to the applied mathematics community?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card--accent">
          <p class="criterion-icon">∑</p>
          <h3 class="criterion-title">Mathematical Correctness &amp; Rigour</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Are proofs, derivations, and computations technically sound? Are assumptions
            clearly stated and conclusions appropriately bounded?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card--accent">
          <p class="criterion-icon">¶</p>
          <h3 class="criterion-title">Clarity &amp; Structure</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Is the paper well-organised, with a clear problem statement, methodology,
            results, and discussion? Is the writing precise and accessible?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card--accent">
          <p class="criterion-icon">⟳</p>
          <h3 class="criterion-title">Reproducibility of Computations</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Are numerical experiments, algorithms, or simulations described with
            sufficient detail for independent replication?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card--accent">
          <p class="criterion-icon">📚</p>
          <h3 class="criterion-title">Appropriate References</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Is the literature review adequate? Are key prior results cited correctly?
            Are citations relevant and properly formatted?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card card--accent">
          <p class="criterion-icon">⊂</p>
          <h3 class="criterion-title">Scope Fit</h3>
          <p class="muted">
            Does the manuscript fall within the aims and scope of AJAM? Would its
            subject matter and level be of interest to our readership?
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─────────────────── Review process & confidentiality ─────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">

      <h2>Review Process &amp; Confidentiality</h2>

      <p>
        AJAM uses <strong>double-blind peer review</strong>: author identities are hidden from
        reviewers, and reviewer identities are hidden from authors throughout the evaluation process.
        This model reduces bias and protects the independence of scholarly judgement.
      </p>

      <p>Reviewers are expected to observe the following obligations:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No contact with authors.</strong> Do not attempt to identify or contact the
          authors of a manuscript assigned to you. All communication must pass through the
          editorial system.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Strict confidentiality.</strong> Manuscripts under review are confidential
          documents. Do not share, cite, or discuss them — in whole or in part — with any
          third party without explicit written permission from the Editor-in-Chief.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Conflict of interest declaration.</strong> If you recognise the authors, have
          a competing interest, or feel unable to provide an impartial assessment for any reason,
          please decline the review immediately via the OJS system and notify the handling editor.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No AI-assisted processing of manuscripts.</strong> Do not upload or paste
          manuscript content into external AI tools (e.g. large language model chatbots).
          Doing so would violate the authors' confidentiality rights and may constitute a
          serious breach of research ethics.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- ─────────────────── Recommendation categories ─────────────────── -->
      <h2>Recommendation Categories</h2>
      <p>
        After completing your review, select one of the following recommendations in the
        OJS submission system. Please ensure your written report justifies the choice.
      </p>

      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Recommendation</th>
            <th>Guidance</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="tag tag--accept">Accept</span></td>
            <td>
              The manuscript is ready for publication as submitted, or requires only
              trivial copy-editing.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="tag tag--minor">Minor revisions</span></td>
            <td>
              The work is fundamentally sound but needs small corrections — typos,
              notation, minor clarifications — that can be verified by the editor.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="tag tag--major">Major revisions</span></td>
            <td>
              The paper has merit but requires substantial reworking — additional proofs,
              experiments, or restructuring — before it can be accepted.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="tag tag--reject">Reject</span></td>
            <td>
              Fundamental flaws (incorrect results, out of scope, insufficient originality)
              that cannot be remedied by revision.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="tag tag--elsewhere">Resubmit elsewhere</span></td>
            <td>
              The manuscript is outside AJAM's scope but may be suitable for a different
              venue; recommend a more appropriate journal if possible.
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- ─────────────────── Writing a constructive report ─────────────────── -->
      <h2>Writing a Constructive Report</h2>
      <p>
        A high-quality review is specific, balanced, and actionable. The following tips
        will help you structure feedback that is genuinely useful to authors and editors alike.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Be specific.</strong> Reference exact sections, equations, or line numbers
          when raising a concern. Vague comments such as "the proof is unclear" are
          difficult for authors to act upon.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Separate major from minor points.</strong> Clearly distinguish issues that
          affect the validity or significance of the work from those that are presentational
          or stylistic.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Maintain a courteous, professional tone.</strong> Critique the work, not
          the authors. Avoid dismissive or condescending language regardless of your
          assessment of the manuscript's quality.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Justify your recommendation.</strong> Your summary recommendation should
          follow logically from the points raised in your report. If you recommend rejection,
          explain concisely why revision cannot address the fundamental deficiencies.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Suggest references judiciously.</strong> You may recommend additional
          literature that would strengthen the paper's context or rigour. Do not use the
          review process to promote your own work; unsolicited self-citation recommendations
          are considered a conflict of interest.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- ─────────────────── Timeline ─────────────────── -->
      <h2>Timeline</h2>

      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Requested review period: 3–4 weeks</strong> from the date of invitation
          acceptance. We recognise that academic schedules vary — if you require an extension,
          please contact the editorial office as early as possible at
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.editorialEmail}`}>{contact.editorialEmail}</a> so
          that we may plan accordingly and avoid undue delays for authors.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are unable to complete the review within an agreed timeframe, kindly notify
          us promptly so the manuscript can be reassigned without further delay.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- ─────────────────── Recognition ─────────────────── -->
      <h2>Recognition</h2>

      <p>
        AJAM acknowledges the invaluable contribution of its reviewers.
        All peer reviewers who complete at least one review in a given calendar year are
        recognised in the annual <em>Acknowledgement of Reviewers</em> published in the
        December issue and on this website.
      </p>

      <p>
        Reviewers may also claim verifiable credit for their service through their OJS
        reviewer records, which can be exported and cited in academic portfolios, grant
        applications, and professional evaluations. To access your review history, log in
        to the submission system and navigate to your reviewer profile.
      </p>

      <div class="center">
        <a href={ojs.login} class="btn btn--primary">Access your reviewer dashboard</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* CTA button row */
  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
  }

  /* Evaluation criterion cards */
  .criterion-icon {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .criterion-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* Recommendation tags */
  .tag--accept   { background: #d1fae5; color: #065f46; }
  .tag--minor    { background: #dbeafe; color: #1e3a8a; }
  .tag--major    { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; }
  .tag--reject   { background: #fee2e2; color: #7f1d1d; }
  .tag--elsewhere { background: #ede9fe; color: #4c1d95; }

  .tag--accept,
  .tag--minor,
  .tag--major,
  .tag--reject,
  .tag--elsewhere {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.2em 0.65em;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
